WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:09.506
Your code has a pipeline: every change runs tests before it ships. Your AI feature? For most teams, it ships on a person clicking around and saying, looks fine.

00:09.506 --> 00:20.223
CI for AI is the same idea, applied to the parts that actually break: prompts, retrieval, and agents. Every change triggers the evaluations and the tests, automatically.

00:20.223 --> 00:28.385
If quality drops, the build goes red and stops — same as a failing unit test. No human has to remember to check. The pipeline remembers for you.

00:28.385 --> 00:34.504
This is the difference between hoping your AI is still good, and knowing it — on every single change.

00:34.504 --> 00:37.319
Put your AI on a pipeline. Let's talk.

